DESCRIPTION:https://events.stanford.edu/event/anastasia-win27-3\n\nRussia\,
  1927. Ten years after the Revolution toppled the Romanov family\, a rumor
  lingers among the people that the youngest royal daughter\, Anastasia\, s
 urvived. We follow a young woman named Anya\, who remembers almost nothing
  of her past\, as she joins a quick-thinking con man and a former aristocr
 at on a journey to Paris to convince the Dowager Empress that Anya is her 
 long-lost granddaughter. With a Soviet officer on their trail and fragment
 s of memory beginning to surface\, Anya must face a question she never exp
 ected: what if the story they have rehearsed is her own?\n\nStanford’s v
 ocalists and instrumentalists present Anastasia\, the 2016 musical inspire
 d by the beloved 1997 animated film\, a story about who we become when the
  past goes missing.\n\nDirected by Ariela Morgenstern\, with Musical Direc
 tor Marie-Louise Catsalis and Vocal Director Benjamin Liupaogo.\n\nBook by
